message: "If you use PandasPlayground in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "PandasPlayground: a reproducible, tested toolkit and curriculum for data manipulation with pandas"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Praveen
    given-names: Satvik
    email: satvikpraveen707@gmail.com
version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-27"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/SatvikPraveen/PandasPlayground"
url: "https://github.com/SatvikPraveen/PandasPlayground"
keywords:
  - pandas
  - data science education
  - reproducibility
  - data validation
  - benchmarking
abstract: >-
  PandasPlayground pairs a ten-notebook pandas curriculum with a typed, tested Python package.
  It provides declarative schema validation, a deterministic pipeline with provenance manifests,
  interval estimates and effect sizes for inference, seeded synthetic data that regenerates
  bit-for-bit, and a benchmark harness that records its environment. Continuous integration
  re-derives every output from raw data and fails on any drift.
